## Getting Started

### 1. Environment Configuration
Copy `.env.example` to `.env`:
```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

### 2. Run the Application
You can run the application directly using standard Go tooling:
```bash
go run ./cmd/serve
```
Or via Go Bootstrap CLI:
```bash
go-bootstrap serve
```

### 3. Endpoints
- `GET /health` - Health check
- `GET /ready` - Readiness check (verifies database connectivity)
- `GET /api/v1/ping` - Ping test
{{- if .HasWorker }}
- `POST /api/v1/jobs` - Enqueue an example background job
{{- end }}

### 4. Build Binary
```bash
go build -o bin/serve ./cmd/serve
```
